  "content": {
    "problemStatement": "An array AAA of length NNN is called good if the sum of all it's elements is non-negative, i.e. (A1+A2+…+AN)≥0(A_1 + A_2 + \\ldots + A_{N}) \\ge 0(A1​+A2​+…+AN​)≥0.\n\nFind the minimum non-negative integer XXX such that if you add XXX to each element of the array, the array becomes good. That is, an array BBB of length NNN, defined as Bi=Ai+XB_i = A_i + XBi​=Ai​+X, is good.\n\n\nInput Format\n\nThe first line of input will contain a single integer TTT, denoting the number of test cases.\nEach test case consists of multiple lines of input.\n\nThe first line of each test case contains a single integer NNN.\nThe second line contains NNN integers - A1,A2,…,ANA_1, A_2, \\ldots, A_NA1​,A2​,…,AN​.\n\n\n\n\nOutput Format\nFor each test case, output on a new line the minimum XXX needed.",
    "constraints": [
      "1≤T≤1001 \\le T \\le 1001≤T≤100",
      "1≤N≤1001 \\le N \\le 1001≤N≤100",
      "−100≤Ai≤100-100 \\le A_i \\le 100−100≤Ai​≤100"
    ],
    "inputFormat": "",
    "outputFormat": "",
    "notes": [],
    "sampleTestCases": [
      {
        "id": "sample_1",
        "type": "reg",
        "input": "4\n3\n1 -5 -3\n2\n-2 -2\n1\n5\n1\n0",
        "output": "3\n2\n0\n0",
        "explanation": "Explanation:\nTest Case 1 : If we add 333 to all elements, we get the array [4,−2,0][4, -2, 0][4,−2,0] which has a sum of 222, a non-negative number. It can be shown that smaller XXX does not satisfy the condition."
      }
    ]
  },
